    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0824" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/12–2049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong Kong</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-20T10:00:00+08:00">December 20,
                            1949—10 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 20—8:05 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 1339. At dinner December 15 S. Y. Liu, former Finance Minister, stated
                    that prior removal of gold stocks from West China <pb facs="0825" n="815"
                        xml:id="pg815"/> to Taiwan approximately 1 million ounces gold stored Taiwan
                    plus 800,000 ounces stored Bank of Taiwan to support currency. Estimated 600,000
                    to 700,000 owners [<hi rendition="#italic">ounces?</hi>] removed from West
                    China.</p>
                <p>Thus at end November total gold holdings of Chinese Government estimated about 2½
                    million ounces. Liu states other types foreign exchange held in negligible
                    amounts only.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
